<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:49.5pt;text-indent:-49.5pt'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=footnote style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For
statutory provisions authorizing county airport districts, see RCW 14.08.290;
for provisions generally regarding municipal airports, see chapters 14.07 and
14.08 RCW.</span></b></p>

<p class=tp><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=footnote style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>CROSS
REFERENCE:  Airport fund, see K.C.C. 4A.200.110.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301792"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.04  DESCRIPTION
OF PROPERTY AND FACILITIES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.04.010     Description of property.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.04.010  Description
of property.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  King County International Airport/Boeing Field (KCIA) is
located five miles south of the center of the city of Seattle.  The elevation is
eighteen feet above mean sea level.  The airport consists of approximately six
hundred acres.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          There are two
parallel runways, described as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          The main runway
(13R/31L) running northwest-southeast is ten thousand feet long and two hundred
feet wide.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          The utility
runway (13L/31R) is three thousand seven hundred ten feet long and one hundred
feet wide.  This runway lies parallel to and three hundred seventy-five feet,
centerline to centerline, east of the main runaway.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          The airport is
owned by King County, Washington [Port of Entry (POE)]*.  KCIA's regional and
national roles are defined by the Federal Aviation Administration in the
National Plan of Integrated Airport Systems Plan.  KCIA is defined as a Class
II primary commercial service (non-hub), general aviation reliever, cargo
service airport.  The airport is a port of Entry.  The control tower is
operated by the Federal Aviation Administration.  The airport is operated on a
seven day-a-week, twenty-four-hour basis, with complete facilities for
servicing large and small aircraft.  (Ord. 16217 § 1, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. I
§ 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Reviser's notes:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>K.C.C. 15.04.010 has been
editorially amended, at the request of the county, in accordance with Ordinance
2315.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Not deleted in Ordinance
16217.  See K.C.C. 1.24.075.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

