letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.08.180     Tower.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.08.190     Undeveloped areas.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.08.200     Business or commerce.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.08.210     Privately owned aircraft.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.08.220     Airport ARFF officer.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.010  Definitions.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The
definitions in this chapter apply throughout this title unless the context
clearly requires otherwise.  Where there is ambiguity in the application of
aviation definitions or terminology the Federal Aviation Administration
Regulations or Advisory Circulars shall provide guidance.  (Ord. 16217 § 2,
2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. II § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.020  B.F.I.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;B.F.I.&quot; means Boeing Field International or King County
International Airport, a public utility operated by King County.  (Ord. 16217 §
3, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. II § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Reviser's Note:  K.C.C.
15.08.020 has been editorially amended, at the request of the county, in
accordance with Ordinance 2315.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.030  Airport.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Airport means King County International Airport/Boeing Field [or BFI or
KCIA]* and comprises all land set aside for King County International Airport. 
BFI is the F.A.A. designation for the airport.  (Ord. 16217 § 4, 2008:  Ord.
1159, Art. II § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Reviser's Notes:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>K.C.C. 15.08.030 has been
editorially amended, at the request of the county, in accordance with Ordinance
2315.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Not underlined in Ordinance
16217.  See K.C.C. 1.24.075.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.040  Airport
manager.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Airport manager&quot; means the airport manager
appointed by the King County executive to manage, superintend, control and
protect the King County International Airport.  (Ord. 16217 § 5, 2008:  Ord.
1159, Art. II § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.050  King
County council.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;King County council&quot; means the King County
council consisting of the duly qualified members holding office under and by
virtue of the provisions of the King County Charter. (Ord. 16217 § 6, 2008:  Ord.
1159, Art. II § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.060  Person.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Person&quot; means any individual, firm, copartnership, corporation,
company, association or joint stock association, and includes any trustee,
receiver, assignee or similar representative thereof.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II § 6,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.070  Aircraft.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Aircraft&quot; is a vehicle used or designed for navigation of or flight
in the air such as any aeroplane, airplane, gas bag, flying machine, balloon,
or any flying contrivance now known or hereafter invented.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II
§ 7, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.080  Main
runway - Utility runway.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Main runway&quot; means runway
13R/31L, and &quot;utility runway&quot; means runway 13L/31R.  (Ord. 1159, Art.
II § 8, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.090  Control
zone.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Control zone&quot; means that airspace of defined
geographical dimensions designated by the F.A.A. above and surrounding Boeing
Field International, within which the airport control tower exercises
authority.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II § 9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.100  F.A.A.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;F.A.A.&quot; means the Federal Aviation Administration of the United
States of America, as defined in the Federal Aviation Act of 1958, as the same
now exists or hereafter be amended.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II § 10, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.105  Federal
obligations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Federal obligations&quot; means federal statutes
and regulations pertaining to the ownership and operation of the airport, grant
agreements between the county and the Federal Aviation Administration,
including, but not limited to, the Airport Improvement Program as authorized by
the Airport and Airway Improvement Act of 1982, as amended, codified as 49
U.S.C.Sec. 47101 et seq, as amended, and the terms, conditions, reservations,
and restrictions prescribed in the Instrument of Transfer, dated May 26, 1948,
between the United States of America and King County, as authorized by the
Surplus Property Act of 1944 (58 Stat.765), codified as 49 U.S.C. Secs.
47151-47153, as amended.  (Ord. 19713 § 1, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.110  Landing
area.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Landing area&quot; means the public use runway
and taxiway system of B.F.I. maintained by the airport for the landing, taking-off
and taxiing by the public, and shall include the areas between the runways and
taxiways and the necessary clearance areas.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II § 11, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.08.115 
Minimum standards.</b>  &quot;Minimum standards&quot; means a document adopted
and formally approved by King County International Airport and reviewed by the
F.A.A., which are detailed provisions defining the minimum standards acceptable
by the county for entities aspiring to conduct commercial or non-commercial
operations or activities on the airport and obligations be met by all who use
or occupy the airport to ensure its safe and efficient operation.  (Ord. 16217
§ 12, 2008).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.120  Operational
areas.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Operational areas&quot; means any place on the
landing area of the airport and shall also include the public use taxiways and
ramps and the necessary rights-of-way and clearance areas therefore, but shall
not include any such areas under lease to a tenant or lessee on B.F.I. (Ord.
16217 § 7, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. II § 12, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.130  Operator.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Operator&quot; means a person who operates aircraft for that person's own
pleasure, passenger service, freight service, hire, charter, flight
instructions, business or test purposes, or who operates an aircraft as a
bailee while performing service on aircraft.  (Ord. 18670 § 69, 2018:  Ord.
1159, Art. II § 13, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.140  Owner.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Owner&quot; means the registered and/or legal owner of an aircraft
according to the files and records of the F.A.A. (Ord. 1159, Art. II § 14,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.150  Ramp.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Ramp&quot; means an area designated as a ramp and used for the parking
and maneuvering, loading and unloading, and servicing of aircraft while they
are on the ground.  &quot;Servicing&quot; of aircraft as used in this code
means only the oiling and fueling thereof.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II § 15, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.160  Road.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Road&quot; means all areas designated as public use roads or streets for
the exclusive use of ground vehicles, including ways open to the public but
shall not include any such areas under lease to a tenant or lessee on the
airport.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II § 16, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.170  Taxiways.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Taxiways&quot; means all areas designated as public use taxiways and used
for the exclusive use of aircraft movement while on the ground, but shall not
include any such areas under lease to a tenant or lessee on the airport.  (Ord.
1159, Art. II § 17, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.180  Tower.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Tower&quot; means the air traffic control tower and the control and
authority established and operated by the F.A.A. for the control of aircraft
and motor vehicle traffic on the operational areas and in the airspace above
and within the B.F.I. [Class D airspace]*.  (Ord. 16217 § 8, 2008:  Ord. 1159,
Art. II § 18, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Not
underlined in accordance with K.C.C. 1.24.075 in Ordinance 16217.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.190  Undeveloped
areas.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Undeveloped areas&quot; means all the land on the
airport except that defined as operational areas and roads, and except that
land legally used by or under lease to a tenant or lessee.  (Ord. 1159, Art. II
§ 19, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.200  Business
or commerce.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Business&quot; or &quot;commerce&quot; means the
use of the airport by any person, group, club, association, or corporation as a
base for conducting commercial activities for the carrying for hire or
compensation of passengers, freight, express or mail, for paid instruction in
aviation or any aviation related field, for the sale of fuels, aviation
supplies and materials, for aircraft rental, sales, maintenance or service, or
for any other aviation or nonaviation commercial activity including the sale of
refreshments or any commodity or service.  (Ord. 16217 § 9, 2008:  Ord. 1159,
Art. II § 20, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.210  Privately
owned aircraft.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Privately owned aircraft&quot; are defined as
aircraft owned individually or by a partnership, or by a nonprofit club or
corporation in which each member must be a bona fide owner or lessee of a part
of the aircraft or of a share in the corporation.  The aircraft shall be owned
and operated for personal, nonrevenue transportation, pleasure or recreational
use only.  (Ord. 16217 § 10, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. II § 21, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.08.220  Airport
ARFF officer.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Airport ARFF officer&quot; means an employed
officer of the airport or airport contractor and holds a commission as a peace
officer in King County, state of Washington.  (Ord. 16217 § 11, 2008:  Ord.
1159, Art. II § 22, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301794"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.12  AIRPORT RULES
AND REGULATIONS IN GENERAL</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.010     Rules and regulations - application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.020     Amendment with due notice.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.030     Enforcement - citation of
violators.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.040     Compliance with rules and regulations.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.050     Restricted areas - authorization
required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.060     Conduct of business, commercial or
noncommercial activity.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.070     Filing location of business with
airport manager - violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.080     Disposal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.090     Damages - responsibility for.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.100     Surface vehicles on operational use
areas.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.110     Removal or impoundment of property.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.12.120     Flying clubs - requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.010  Rules
and regulations - application.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The rules and
regulations hereinafter set forth, and all orders, instructions, rules, minimum
standards and regulations promulgated under authority herein prescribed, shall
apply to and be in full force and effect upon B.F.I. as it is now or may
hereafter be constituted, and all persons using the facilities of B.F.I. shall
observe same and such observance shall be a condition under which all persons
may use such facilities.  (Ord. 16217 § 13, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. III § 1,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.020  Amendment
with due notice.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The King County council reserves the right to revise,
delete, amend, or add to any of these regulations or rules with due notice. 
(Ord. 1159, Art. III § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.030  Enforcement
- citation of violators.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The provisions of this title and any
resolutions, minimum standards or other rules and regulations promulgated under
this title, and the provisions of any other ordinance or law, the violation of
which constitutes an infraction or violation, pertaining to the conduct of
persons upon or about, or to operations of, B.F.I., may be enforced in any
manner provided for by law.  (Ord. 16217 § 14, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. III § 3,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.040  Compliance
with rules and regulations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All persons using the facilities of
B.F.I. shall be governed by the rules and regulations herein prescribed and by
the provisions of the King County Code.  (Ord. 1159, Art. III § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.050  Restricted
areas - authorization required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person other than
those in an aircraft operating on the airport or in vehicles authorized to
service or support such aircraft shall enter the operational area unless with
approval of the airport manager or designee.  All persons authorized access to
the operational areas shall have suitable identification on them when in the
area.  (Ord. 16217 § 15, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. III § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.060  Conduct
of business, commercial or noncommercial activity.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
No person may solicit, offer for sale or hire or sell or engage in any business
or commercial or noncommercial activity of any nature on or from the airport
except from a fixed place of business or operation and in conformance with an
appropriate lease or permit or as provided in the rules and regulations.  (Ord.
16217 § 16, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. III § 6, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.070  Filing
location of business with airport manager - violation.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
All airport business or commercial operators must file with the airport manager
the name and location on the airport of their business, and if any change in
name, ownership and location is made, notice of such change must be given to
the airport manager immediately.  Failure to notify the airport manager shall
constitute a violation of the airport rules and regulations, and will subject
the operator to the penalties thereof.  (Ord. 16217 § 17, 2008:  Ord. 1159,
Art. III § 7, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.080  Disposal.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
No person shall deposit substances on B.F.I. which may cause damage or be a
nuisance or a hazard to persons or property.  No person shall place, dispose or
deposit in any manner trash, garbage, material, debris or refuse in or upon the
operational areas, undeveloped areas, or roads except at such places and under
such conditions as the airport manager may from time to time prescribe.  (Ord.
16217 § 18, 2008: Ord. 1159, Art. III § 8, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.090  Damages
- responsibility for.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any and all airport property destroyed, injured, or
damaged shall be paid for by the person or persons responsible for such
destruction, injury, or damage thereto.  (Ord. 1159, Art. III § 9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.100  Surface
vehicles on operational use areas.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No surface vehicles
other than aircraft and fueling and flight line service vehicles shall be
operated on the operational areas except those specifically authorized by the
airport manager.  Each vehicle authorized access to operational areas shall
display visual identification (such as a large decal or sign) while operating
in that area.  (Ord. 1159, Art. III § 10, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.110  Removal
or impoundment of property.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The airport manager or designee may
remove and impound from any area of the airport including leased premises any
motor vehicle, aircraft or other property that causes or constitutes or
reasonably appears to cause or constitute an imminent or immediate danger to
the health or safety of the persons using the airport or a significant portion
thereof.  The airport manager or designee may also remove or impound from any
area of the airport, including leased premises any motor vehicle, aircraft or
other property due to lack of payment for leasehold, parking or storage,
airport fees and assessments or abandonment of property at the end of a lease
term or termination of a lease, if the lessee is in default pursuant to the
terms of the lease.  Such vehicles, aircraft or other property may be disposed
of through sell, surplus, auction or other action in accordance with the
guidance provided in RCW 14.08.122.  Vehicles, equipment and other property
abandoned in the parking areas or any other areas of the airport may be
impounded and removed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          The expenses of
such a removal and any storage fees shall become a lien chargeable to the owner
of motor vehicle, aircraft or other property.  The owner shall be notified of
the removal and storage of motor vehicle, aircraft or other property by
certified or registered mail with a five-day return requested, sent to the
owner's address as known to the airport manager or the manager's designee,
within three days of said removal and storage.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          The removal from
any area of the airport including leased premises of any motor vehicle,
aircraft or other property constituting a nuisance or which is disabled,
abandoned or in violation of this code but which does not cause or constitute
an imminent or immediate danger to the health or safety of the persons using
the airport or a significant portion thereof shall be accomplished in
accordance with the procedure in chapters 7.48 and 46.55 RCW.  (Ord. 16217 §
19, 2008: Ord. 1159, Art. III § 11, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.12.120  Flying
clubs - requirements.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  A flying
club must be organized as a nonprofit corporation under the laws of the state
of Washington or of the United States for the purpose of fostering flying for
pleasure, developing skills in aviation, and developing an awareness and
appreciation of aviation requirements and techniques to the general public.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Each club
must furnish to the airport manager a current and correct copy of the bylaws,
articles of incorporation, operating rules and membership agreements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  A current
certified roster of officers and directors and their addresses must be filed
annually with the airport manager.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  The
commercial use of B.F.I. by flying clubs is prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  The flying
club shall maintain a membership record containing the full names, addresses
and pilot license number and rating of all active members, together with the
date when their membership commenced.  These records shall be certified by an
officer of the flying club and made available for inspection at any reasonable
time upon request of and by the airport manager or designee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  All flying
clubs will submit to the airport manager upon the airport manager's request a
certified list of all instructors who are or have been instructing members of
the club and the names of each of the members who received said instruction and
the dates and time duration of such instruction within the six months preceding
the request.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          G.  All flying
clubs must obtain public liability and property damage insurance with a hold
harmless agreement in favor of B.F.I. and King County, its officers and
employees.  King County's office of risk management services shall assess the
insurance requirements and provide a determination of liability and amount of
insurance needed.  Certificates of insurance will be kept on file at all times
with the airport manager.  Thirty days' prior notice of cancellation shall also
be filed with the airport manager.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          H.  All aircraft
owned, leased or used by the club must first be registered with the airport
manager.  Club aircraft shall not be used for business or commercial
activities.  (</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
color:black'>Ord. 19015 </span><span lang=DE style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'> 10, 2019: 
</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>Ord. 18670 § 70, 2018:  Ord. 16217 § 20, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. III §
12, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301795"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.16  AIRCRAFT
OPERATIONS</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.010     Aircraft operation and maintenance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.020     Brakes required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.030     Aircraft storage - Repairs.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.040     Securing of unattended aircraft.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.050     Parking of aircraft.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.060     Postponing and delaying of airport
operations.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.070     Use of intoxicants and drugs.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.080     Disabled aircraft.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.090     Charges for moving disabled
aircraft - liability.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.100     Noise and slipstreams.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.110     Starting and running of aircraft
engines.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.120     Instructor responsibility.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.140     Parking gate assignment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.16.150     Nighttime landings - Maximum
number.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.010  Aircraft
operation and maintenance.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall navigate, land, fly,
service, move, maintain, or repair any aircraft, nor conduct any aviation
activities, upon, on or from the airport other than in conformity with current
F.A.A. rules and regulations established under federal authority, including all
current air traffic rules as established by the airport and F.A.A. and
controlled by the B.F.I. control tower.  Navigation lights shall be lighted on
all aircraft moving on the taxiways and ramps of the airport from dusk to
daylight, including aircraft under tow.  (Ord. 3382 § 1, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art.
IV § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.020  Brakes
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No aircraft may be operated at the airport unless it is
equipped with satisfactory and usable brakes.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.030  Aircraft
storage - Repairs.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Aircraft shall be stored and repairs shall be made only
on the leased sites where permitted, and there shall be aircraft storage but no
repair work on the public use ramps.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.040  Securing
of unattended aircraft.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No aircraft shall be left unattended
on any area of the airport, including leased premises, unless properly
secured.  The securing of aircraft shall be the sole responsibility of the
owner or operator of the aircraft, and B.F.I. and its officers, employees, and
agents shall be in no way held responsible.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.050  Parking
of aircraft.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Except for parking and servicing of aircraft where
permitted on public use ramps, provisions for parking all aircraft by any
operator, user, tenant or its patrons, invitees, employees and others, shall be
on leased premises where permitted and off the operational area of the
airport.  No holding, stopping or parking of aircraft on the taxiways shall be
permitted other than to gain immediate ingress or egress of the aircraft from
or to adjacent premises, unless directed by the F.A.A. and under air traffic
control.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          Unairworthy
aircraft, wrecks, &quot;junkers&quot; or parts thereof shall not be parked or
stored anywhere on the airport or leased sites unless awaiting bona fide
scheduled repairs by a bona fide commercial aviation business on the airport,
unless express authority is granted by the airport manager.  (Ord. 16217 § 21,
2008: Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.060  Postponing
and delaying of airport operations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The manager of the
airport may delay or restrict any flight or other operations at the airport for
any emergency or other cause, the ramifications of which indicate danger to the
public or impending violation of rules and regulations applicable to such
flight or other operations.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 6, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.070  Use
of intoxicants and drugs.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  The
following persons shall not be under the influence of any intoxicating
substance that renders the person incapable of safely performing the persons'
duties:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  A pilot or
other member of the crew of an aircraft in operation on the airport or
indicating intent to do so; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  A person
directly attending or assisting in the operation on the airport.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  A person who
is a passenger of an aircraft in operation on the airport or intending to be a
passenger shall not be under the influence of any intoxicating substance to a
degree that would endanger the safety of any persons using the airport.  (Ord.
18670 § 71, 2018:  Ord. 16217 § 22, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 7, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.080 
Disabled aircraft.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Each aircraft owner, or the owner's pilot or agent,
shall be responsible for the prompt removal of disabled aircraft and parts
thereof unless required or directed to delay such action pending an
investigation of an accident.  (Ord. 16217 § 23, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 8,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.090  Charges
for moving disabled aircraft - liability.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Should pilots,
owners or agents authorize airport employees to remove disabled aircraft from
runways, ramps, taxiways or other operational or other areas on the airport,
charges will be made for equipment and personnel at currently established
prices and rates.  Neither the airport nor King County, nor both the airport
and King County, accept liability for removal of aircraft.  (Ord. 16217 § 24,
2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.100  Noise
and slipstreams.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No aircraft shall be operated in such a manner or in
such places, in front of or near hangers, shops, buildings, personal property,
or persons so that they are in the propeller slipstream or jet blast so that
the operation creates a hazard or a nuisance.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 10, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.110  Starting
and running of aircraft engines.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Except aircraft under
the control of authorized maintenance shops, no aircraft engine shall be
started or run unless a licensed pilot or mechanic is attending the controls. 
Chocks shall be placed in front of the main gear wheels before starting engine
or engines unless the aircraft is equipped with and is using adequate parking
brakes.  (Ord. 16217 § 25, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 11, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.120  Instructor
responsibility.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Instructors shall meet F.A.A. criteria for
certification.  Instructors shall fully acquaint their students with these
rules and regulations and shall be responsible for the conduct of students
under their direction during dual instructions.  When the student is flying
solo, it shall be the student's sole responsibility to observe and abide by
these rules and regulations.  (Ord. 16217 § 26, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. IV § 12,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.140  Parking
gate assignment.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Aircraft parking at Terminal Building gates and other
public use ramps shall be assigned by the airport manager, or designee, and
aircraft so assigned shall park in accordance with the assignment.  (Ord. 16217
§ 28, 2008:  Ord. 3382 § 3, 1977).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.16.150  Nighttime
landings - Maximum number.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No aircraft may perform &quot;touch
and go landings&quot; (i.e., an operation by an aircraft that lands and departs
on a runway without stopping or exiting the runway) during a nighttime period. 
For purposes of this section, &quot;nighttime period&quot; means a period
commencing at ten p.m. and ending at seven a.m. the following day.  In
addition, all nighttime flight activities shall be restricted to the west
runway (31L &#8209; 13R).  No nighttime flight operations shall take place on
the east runway (31R &#8209; 13L).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          Nothing in this
section shall be deemed to prevent the Federal Aviation Administration Air
Traffic Control tower from utilizing any runway at any time to ensure the safe
operation of aircraft.  (Ord. 4448 § 1, 1979).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301796"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.20  AIRCRAFT &#8209;
GENERALLY</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.20.010     Scope of chapter - Exceptions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.20.020     Compliance with rules and
regulations.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.20.030     Adoption of Federal Aviation
Administration rules.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.20.040     Two-way radio required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.20.050     Radio procedures and frequencies.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.20.060     Engine warm-up and runup places - propeller
slipstream or jet blast.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.20.010  Scope
of chapter - Exceptions.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  This chapter shall govern the
conduct of all persons engaged in aeronautical activities at B.F.I., or while
flying in the B.F.I. traffic zone, unless exceptions are specifically provided
for in federal air regulations, or unless exceptions not in conflict with
federal air regulations are authorized by the airport manager.  (Ord. 1159,
Art. V § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.20.020  Compliance
with rules and regulations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall navigate any
aircraft, land upon, fly same from, service, maintain, repair any aircraft, or
conduct any aircraft operations on or from B.F.I., otherwise than in conformity
with all current federal, state, county rules and regulations including those
rules and regulations established from time to time by the airport manager.  (Ord.
16217 § 29, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. V § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.20.030  Adoption
of Federal Aviation Administration rules.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The air traffic
rules as established by the F.A.A., and currently in effect, are adopted and
made a part of these rules as fully as if the same and each were set forth
herein.  (Ord. 1159, Art. V § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.20.040  Two-way
radio required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No aircraft may land or take off unless it is equipped
with functioning two&#8209;way radio capable of two-way communication with
B.F.I. air traffic control tower, except in case of emergencies.  Two-way radio
communication with B.F.I. air traffic control tower shall be provided for all
aircraft movements on the operational areas of the airport including, but not
limited to, aircraft in tow.  (Ord. 3382 § 4, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art. V § 4,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.20.050  Radio
procedures and frequencies.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All radio transmission shall be in
accordance with the procedure prescribed by the Federal Communications
Commission.  (Ord. 1159, Art. V § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.20.060  Engine
warm-up or runup places - propeller slipstream or jet blast.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Aircraft engines may be started or warmed up, or engine runups performed, only
in the places designated for such purposes by the airport manager.  Caution
must be exercised at all times to protect persons and property from the
propeller slipstream or jet blast.  (Ord. 16217 § 30, 2008: Ord. 1159, Art. V §
6, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301797"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.24  PUBLIC USE OF
ROADS, WALKS AND FACILITIES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.010     Restricted areas.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.020     Restricted areas - impoundment and removal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.030     Obstructions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.040     Type of vehicles.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.050     Liability of county for injury.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.060     Liquor and narcotics.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.070     Lost articles.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.24.080     Animals.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.010  Restricted
areas.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person or persons shall loiter in public areas on
the airport for purpose of soliciting aircraft rides.  No person shall enter
any restricted area posted as being closed to the public, except:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Persons
assigned to duty thereon;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Persons
authorized by the airport manager;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  Passengers
under appropriate supervision entering the apron for the purpose of embarkation
and debarkation to and from aircraft.  (Ord. 3382 § 5, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art. VI
§ 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.020  Restricted
areas - impoundment and removal.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall travel
or drive on the airport other than on the roads or places provided for that
purpose and no vehicle shall be parked on any area other than those areas
designated by the airport manager.  Vehicles in violation of designated parking
and travel areas shall be subject to ticketing or towing at the owner's
expense. Vehicles, equipment and other property abandoned in the parking areas
or any other areas of the airport may be impounded and removed.  (Ord. 16217 §
31, 2008:  Ord. 3382 § 6, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art. VI § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.030  Obstructions.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
No person shall use the roads, walks or other thoroughfares in such manner as
to hinder or obstruct their proper use.  (Ord. 1159, Art. VI § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.040  Type
of vehicles.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The airport manager may prohibit from roads, walks and
paved areas any type of vehicle equipped with other than pneumatic tires and
other vehicles or equipment whose operation would damage said roads, walks and
paved areas.  (Ord. 1159, Art. VI § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.050  Liability
of county for injury.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  King County assumes no responsibility for injury or
damage to persons or property of persons, stored on, or using the airport
facilities, by reason of fire, theft, vandalism, weather, storm, flood,
earthquake, and collision, nor does it assume any liability by reason of injury
to persons while on the airport or while using the facilities of same.  (Ord.
1159, Art. VI § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.060  Liquor
and narcotics.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person under the influence of liquor or narcotic
drugs shall be allowed on the operational areas of the airport.  Liquor shall
not be consumed in any public area on the airport except in those places of
business in possession of a valid Washington State Liquor Control Board
permit.  (Ord. 3382 § 7, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art. VI § 6, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.070  Lost
articles.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person finding lost articles shall deposit them at
the office of the airport manager or airport air rescue fire fighting office. 
(Ord. 16217 § 32, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. VI § 7, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.24.080  Animals.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
All animals shall be on a leash or caged and shall not be allowed on the
operational areas of the airport.  Any domestic animal found to be roaming free
on airport property will be subject to impounding by the county animal
authority.  (Ord. 16217 § 33, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. VI § 8, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301798"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.28  ACCIDENTS AND
SAFETY</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.28.010     Report of accidents.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.28.020     Report of hazardous conditions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.28.030     Accidents on airport - closure.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.28.010  Report
of accidents.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person involved in any accident on the airport, and
all witnesses thereto, shall report to the airport manager's office or to the
airport air rescue fire fighting office immediately.  (Ord. 16217 § 34, 2008:  Ord.
1159, Art. VII § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.28.020  Report
of hazardous conditions.</b>  Any person observing a condition or hazard that
would jeopardize life, health, public safety, or damage to property, should
report same to the airport manager's office or airport operations office or airport
air rescue fire fighting office immediately.  (Ord. 16217 § 35, 2008:  Ord.
1159, Art. VII § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.28.030  Accidents
on airport - closure.</b>  In case of an accident on the airport, the airport
may be closed to air operations and the public in order not to hamper the
rescue or recovery operations.  (Ord. 16217 § 36, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. VII §
3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301799"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.32  RULES OF
CONDUCT</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.32.010     Disorderly conduct.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.32.020     Garbage and refuse.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.32.030     Care of property.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.32.040     Firearms, explosives and
inflammable materials - prohibited - exceptions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.32.010  Disorderly
conduct.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall commit any disorderly or unlawful act
or commit any nuisance on the airport.  (Ord. 1159, Art. VIII § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.32.020  Garbage
and refuse.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Garbage, papers and refuse, or other material, shall be
placed in covered receptacles ordinarily used for such purposes.  (Ord. 1159,
Art. VIII § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.32.030  Care
of property.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Destroy,
injure, deface, or disturb in any way, any property, sign, structure, or other
public property on the airport;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  Trespass on
lawns and seeded areas or public art work on the airport;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  Abandon any
personal property on the airport.  (Ord. 16217 § 37, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art.
VIII § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.32.040  Firearms,
explosives and inflammable materials - prohibited - exceptions.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
No person shall carry any firearms, explosives or flammable materials on the
airport in any other manner than that provided by law, except by written
permission of the airport manager.  (Ord. 16217 § 38, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art.
VIII § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301800"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.36  MOTOR VEHICLE
REGULATIONS</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.010     Speed limits - nonmotorized
vehicles - enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.020     Compliance with parking signs -
ticketing - towing.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.030     Employee parking.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.040     Passenger loading.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.050     Areas permitted to motor equipment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.060     Perimeter road.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.070     Pedestrians.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.080     Compliance with signs.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.090     Compliance with code - Emergency
provision.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.36.100     Vehicle parking rates.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.010  Speed
limits - nonmotorized vehicles - enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The maximum speed
limit in all vehicular areas on the airport is twenty miles per hour, unless
otherwise posted.  Speed limit for vehicles operating in the airport
operational area shall be fifteen miles per hour.  Bicycles, skateboards and
nonmotorized vehicles are prohibited on the airport airside service road,
operations area and sidewalks.  Airport operations office and the ARFF unit
shall enforce all traffic regulations in accordance with the King County
Traffic Code, K.C.C. Title 46.  (Ord. 16217 § 39, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. IX §
9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.020  Compliance
with parking signs - ticketing - towing.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Vehicles shall not be
parked on the airport other than in the manner and at parking areas indicated
by posted traffic signs and curb markings. Vehicles in violation of designated
parking and travel areas shall be subject to ticketing or towing at the owner's
expense.  (Ord. 16217 § 40, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. IX § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.030  Employee
parking.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Personnel employed on the airport shall park only in
employee parking areas as designated by the airport manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art.
IX § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.040  Passenger
loading.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No common carrier vehicle or vehicle for hire shall
load or unload passengers at the airport other than in the area so designated
as passenger loading zones.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IX § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.050  Areas
permitted to motor equipment.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No motorized equipment
shall be operated on the apron of the terminal building, or other areas not
designated for vehicular traffic, except those authorized by the airport
manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IX § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.060  Perimeter
road.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The Perimeter Road, as posted, shall be closed to all
traffic except: official cars or trucks, or cars and trucks traveling on
airport business, or those cars or trucks with written permission of the
airport manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IX § 6, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.070  Pedestrians.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Pedestrians shall have the right-of-way over vehicular traffic and shall use pedestrian
lanes wherever provided.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IX § 7, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.080  Compliance
with signs.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All vehicles shall be operated in accordance with all
posted signs and pavement markings.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IX § 8, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.36.090  Compliance
with code - Emergency provision.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Motor vehicles shall be
operated on the airport in strict accordance with the foregoing rules
prescribed by the King County council and airport manager for the control of
such vehicles, except in the case of emergency involving danger to life and
property.  (Ord. 1159, Art. IX § 9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.36.100 
Vehicle parking rates.</b>  Vehicle parking rates may be implemented at King
County International Airport at such a time when annual passenger enplanements
exceed one hundred thousand or market conditions warrant.  Vehicle parking
rates shall be set by the airport manager to reflect fair market value.  The
airport may also contract for parking services with a parking service
provider.  All parking rates shall include applicable sales and use tax.  These
rates are subject to change without notice.  (Ord. 16244 § 2, 2008:  Ord. 16217
§ 41, 2008 [repealed by 16244, § 12, 2008]:  Ord. 1159, Art IX § 10, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301801"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.40  FUELING AND
FUEL STORAGE</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.010     General safety.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.020     Fueling while engine is running or
in enclosed places prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.030     Smoking prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.040     Electronic or electrical equipment
to remain off.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.050     Grounding of electrical potential.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.060     Prevention of overflow.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.070     Attendant and stairs.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.080     Personnel permitted.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.090     Static spark materials.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.100     Fire extinguishers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.110     Fuel spills - starting engine
prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.120     Equipment maintenance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.130     Grounding device.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.140     Distance from buildings.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.150     Smoking prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.160     Equipment routes and parking.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.40.170     Fire requirements for equipment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.010  General
safety.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person in or upon any areas where fueling or
defueling is being conducted shall do or fail to do any act if the doing or
omission thereof endangers unreasonably or is likely to endanger unreasonably
persons or property.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.020  Fueling
while engine is running or in enclosed places prohibited.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
No aircraft shall be fueled or drained of fuel while the engine is running or
while such aircraft is in a hangar or enclosed space. (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 2,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.030  Smoking
prohibited.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The airport is a smoke free public facility.  There is
a no smoking on any public or leasehold ramps or other aircraft movement areas. 
(Ord. 16217 § 42, 2008:  Ord. 3382 § 8, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art. X § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.040  Electronic
and electrical equipment to remain off.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall operate
any radio transmitter or receiver, or switch electrical appliances off or on in
an aircraft during fueling or draining of fuel.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.050  Grounding
of electrical potential.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  During refueling the aircraft and
the fuel dispensing apparatus shall both be grounded and bonded to a point or
points of zero electrical potential.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.060  Prevention
of overflow.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Persons engaged in the fueling and draining of aircraft
shall exercise care to prevent overflow of fuel.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 6,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.070  Attendant
and stairs.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No passenger or passengers shall be permitted in any
aircraft during fueling or defueling unless an aircraft attendant and passenger
stairs are present at or near each cabin door ordinarily used by enplaning or
deplaning passengers.  (Ord. 16217 § 43, 2008:  Ord. 3382 § 9, 1977: Ord. 1159,
Art. X § 7, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.080  Personnel
permitted.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Only personnel engaged in the fueling, maintenance, and
operation of an aircraft shall be permitted within one hundred feet of fuel
tanks of such aircraft during any such operation.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 8,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.090  Static
spark materials.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall use any material during fueling or
draining of fuel from aircraft which is likely to cause a static discharge. 
(Ord. 1159, Art. X § 9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.100  Fire
extinguishers.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Adequate fire extinguishers shall be within ready reach
of personnel engaged in fueling and draining operations.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X §
10, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.110  Fuel
spills - starting engine prohibited.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall start
the engine of any aircraft when there is aviation gasoline, JetA fuel or
gasoline on the ground under or nearby such aircraft.  (Ord. 16217 § 45, 2008: 
Ord. 1159, Art. X § 11, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.120  Equipment
maintenance.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Fueling hoses and draining equipment shall be
maintained in a safe, sound and nonleaking condition.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 12,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.130  Grounding
device.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All hoses, funnels, and appurtenances used in fueling
and draining operations shall be equipped with a grounding device to prevent
ignition of volatile liquids.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X § 13, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.140  Distance
from buildings.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The fueling and draining of aircraft fuel shall be
conducted at a safe distance from any hangar or other building.  (Ord. 16217 §
45, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. X § 14, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.150  Smoking
prohibited.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The airport is a smoke free public facility.  There is
no smoking on any public or leasehold ramps or other aircraft movement areas. 
(Ord. 16217 § 46, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. X § 15, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.160  Equipment
routes and parking.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Routes for fueling equipment and parking areas for
fueling points will be designated by the airport manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art. X §
16, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.40.170  Fire
requirements for equipment.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Fueling equipment must be equipped
to fully meet all fire regulation requirements and shall comply with all
existing fire regulations including an authorized permit properly affixed and
displayed on full dispensing equipment.  (Ord. 3382 § 10, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art.
X § 17, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301802"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.44  FIRE
REGULATIONS</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.44.010     Construction or alteration of
buildings.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.44.020     Cleaning with flammable liquids.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.44.030     Open flame operations.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.44.040     Storage of material and equipment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.44.050     Storage of flammable liquids.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.44.010  Construction
or alteration of buildings.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All construction, maintenance,
alterations of buildings, structures and shelters shall be done in conformance
with the building and fire codes, and on approval of the airport manager. 
(Ord. 1159, Art. XI § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.44.020  Cleaning
with flammable liquids.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall use flammable
volatile liquids in the cleaning of aircraft, aircraft engines, propellers, appliances
or facilities unless such cleaning operations are conducted in open air, or in
a properly ventilated room specifically set aside for that purpose, which room
must be properly fireproofed and equipped with adequate and readily accessible
fire extinguishing apparatus. (Ord. 16217 § 47, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. XI § 2,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.44.030  Open
flame operations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall conduct any open flame operation in any
hangar or on the airport grounds, or part thereof, unless specifically
authorized by the airport manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XI § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.44.040  Storage
of material and equipment.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall store or stock
material or equipment on the airport in such manner as to constitute a fire
hazard.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XI § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.44.050  Storage
of flammable liquids.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person shall keep or store any flammable liquids,
gases, signal flares, or other similar materials in the hangars or in any
building on the airport; provided, that such materials may be kept in an
aircraft in the proper receptacles installed in the aircraft for such purposes
or in rooms or areas specifically approved for such storage by the airport
manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XI § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301803"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.48  TAXICABS,
LIMOUSINES AND FOR HIRE AUTOMOBILE SERVICE COMPANIES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>(Formerly TAXICAB
OPERATING AGREEMENT)</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.48.010     Taxicabs' fee for privilege of
operating at B.F.I.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.48.020     Authority of airport manager to
terminate operating agreements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.48.030     Taxicab companies to conform to
regulations.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.48.040     Fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.48.050     Operating agreement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-1.5in'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.48.010  Taxicabs'
fee for privilege of operating at B.F.I.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All taxicabs desiring to
provide service from B.F.I. shall be charged a fee established by King County
for the right and privilege to provide service from B.F.I.  An appropriate
sticker shall be conspicuously displayed as prescribed by the airport on each
taxicab.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XII § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.48.020  Authority
of airport manager to terminate operating agreements.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The airport manager shall have the right to terminate taxicab operating
agreements for violations of rules and regulations and terms and conditions of
the agreement.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XII § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.48.030  Taxicab
companies to conform to regulations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All taxicab companies desiring
to provide service from B.F.I. must conform with the requirements of the proper
governmental authority which has jurisdiction over such regulation of
taxicabs.  All taxicab companies  must comply with the regulations in effect at
B.F.I.  (Ord. 16217 § 48, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. XII § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.48.040 
Fees.</b>  All taxicab, limousine or for hire automobile service companies
providing service from B.F.I. pursuant to the terms and conditions stated in
K.C.C. chapter 15.48 shall pay to the airport five hundred dollars per calendar
year for an operating agreement by the airport.  Such operating agreements
shall be required when annual airport passenger enplanements exceed one hundred
thousand or F.A.A. Part 121 commercial air service is approved.  No fee shall
be charged by the airport for the delivery of passengers to the airport.  (Ord.
16244 § 3, 2008:  Ord. 16217 § 49, 2008 [repealed by 16244 § 12, 2008]:  Ord.
1159, Art. XX § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.48.050  Operating
agreement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The agreement as referred to in Chapter 15.48 of this
title shall be in a form as prescribed by the airport and the fee specified in
Section 15.48.040 above shall be remitted upon application for an operating
agreement.  The fee will not be prorated for a portion of the calendar year in
which the operating agreement is issued.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XX § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>CROSS REFERENCE:  Taxis &#8209;
Businesses and Drivers, see K.C.C. chapter 6.64.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301804"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.52  SCHEDULE OF
FEES, RENTALS, RATES, CHARGES AND GENERAL CONDITIONS</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.010     Rentals, rates, charges and
conditions for use of the airport.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.020     Current rates.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.030     Revision of rates and charges.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.040     Delinquent payments.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.050     Establishment of rates and charges.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.060     Charges.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.065     Market rental rate or charge for
facilities use.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.52.090     Payment of fees - when - penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.52.010  Rentals,
rates, charges and conditions for use of the airport.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Rentals,
rates, charges and conditions for use of the airport and its public facilities
shall be those specified in this chapter and may be amended from time to time
by the King County council.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XIII § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.52.020  Current
rates.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A complete copy of all existing, current rates, fees
and charges applicable to B.F.I. is available upon request from the office of
the airport manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XIII § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.52.030  Revision
of rates and charges.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The King County council reserves the right to revise,
delete, amend, or add to these schedule of fees, rentals, rates, charges, and
general conditions with due notice.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XIII § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.52.040  Delinquent
payments.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person determined to be delinquent in the person's
payment for the use of airport facilities may be promptly removed from the
airport by or under the authority of the airport manager, and may be deprived
of, or refused the further use of, the airport and its facilities.  (Ord. 18670
§ 72, 2018:  Ord. 1159, Art. XIII § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.52.050  Establishment
of rates and charges.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The airport manager, with approval of the King County
council, may establish charges or rates not covered by the schedule of fees. 
(Ord. 1159, Art. XIII § 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.52.060 
Charges.</b>  Charges shall be made for storage of aircraft on county property,
except that short-term, transient aircraft parking provided adjacent to the
terminal building for aircraft weighing zero to twelve thousand five hundred
pounds shall be free for the first hour.  The pilot shall notify the airport
operations office upon arrival.  All other aircraft parking shall have the
rates specified in K.C.C. 4A.700.850.  (Ord. 18293 § 1, 2016:  Ord. 17919 § 2,
2014:  Ord. 16244 § 4, 2008:  Ord. 16217 § 50, 2008 [repealed by 16244 § 12,
2008]: Ord. 16025 § 2, 2008:  Ord. 15639 § 2, 2006:  Ord. 15315 § 2, 2005: 
Ord. 10500 § 1, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.52.065 
Market rental rate or charge for facilities use.  </b>All airport facilities
used by the general public, tenants and public and private organizations,
including governmental units and agencies, may be assessed a market rental rate
or charge for the use of facilities.  For the purpose of this section, &quot;facilities&quot;
include, but are not limited to, rooms, public areas, parking lots, aircraft
ramps and terminal building as well as water, storm water or other utility
systems.  (Ord. 17919 § 4, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.52.090 
Payment of fees - when - penalties.</b>  Payment of monthly fees is due and
payable in advance on the first day of each calendar month.  Payment of daily
parking fees shall be made prior to departure of aircraft, unless arrangements
have been approved by the airport manager.  Airport late fees and penalties
shall be assessed in the amount of one and one-half percent per month for
unpaid rates, charges or fees.  Failure to pay airport rates, charges and fees
or rents may, at the sole discretion of the airport manager, result in a loss
of use of airport facilities and legal action to recover unpaid rates, charges
or fees.  (Ord. 16244 § 5, 2008: Ord. 16217 § 53, 2008 [repealed by 16244 § 12,
2008]: Ord. 1159, Art XIII § 9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301805"><span style='font-size:12.0pt;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>15.56  </span></a><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>AVIATION FUEL SALES - FIELD USE FEES</span></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.56.010     Charge on company selling or
delivering fuel - monthly report - penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.56.010  Charge
on company selling or delivering fuel - monthly report - penalties.</b>  Oil
companies or fuel distributor companies, or both, engaged in the business of
selling or delivering aviation fuel to any individual, business firm, United
States government or organization on B.F.I., or selling aviation fuel to any
individual, business firm, United States government or organization to be used
in aircraft located on or being serviced to take off from B.F.I., shall pay a
fuel field use fee charge in an amount specified in K.C.C. 4A.700.860.A.  This
charge shall be collected by the oil companies or fuel distributor companies,
or both, making the sale or delivery and reported in a form prescribed by and
acceptable to the airport manager with remittance made to the airport on or before
the twentieth of each month.  Airport late fees and penalties shall be assessed
in the amount specified in K.C.C. 4A.700.860.B.  Failure to pay airport rates,
charges and fees or rents may, at the sole discretion of the airport manager,
result in a loss of use of airport facilities and legal action to recover
unpaid rates, charges or fees.  (Ord. 17919 § 5, 2014:  Ord. 16244 § 6, 2008: 
Ord. 16217 § 54, 2008 [repealed by Ord. 16244, § 12, 2008]:  Ord. 15639 § 4,
2006:  Ord. 15315 § 4, 2005:  Ord. 15061 § 4, 2004:  Ord. 6246 § 2, 1982:  Ord.
3382 § 13, 1977:  Ord. 1159, Art. XIV § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301806"><span style='font-size:12.0pt;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>15.60  </span></a><span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>PAYMENT - LANDING, TIE-DOWN AND OTHER FEES</span></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.60.010     Payment - lien.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.60.010 
Payment - lien.</b>  No person shall allow any aircraft owned by the person or
under the person's control to land, take off, use B.F.I. facilities or be
parked or tied down on B.F.I. without causing all applicable landing, tie-down
or other fees respecting such aircraft or use of B.F.I. facilities to be paid. 
Any such fees that become due and owing shall constitute a lien on such
aircraft.  Airport late fees and penalties shall be assessed in the amount of
one and one-half percent per month for unpaid rates, charges or fees.  Failure
to pay airport rates, charges and fees or rents may, at the sole discretion of
the airport manager, result in either a loss of use of airport facilities or
legal action to recover unpaid rates, charges or fees, or both the loss of use
and legal action.  (Ord. 16244 § 7, 2008:  Ord. 16217 § 55, 2008 [repealed by
Ord. 16244, § 12, 2008]:  Ord. 3382 § 16, 1977:  Ord. 1159, Art XV § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301807"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.64  OPERATIONS OF
AIRCRAFT - APPLICATION OF CHARGES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.64.020     Landing fees - penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.64.030     Monthly report.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.64.040     Payment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.64.050     Schedule defined.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.64.060     Passenger terminal user fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.64.070     Landing fees - exemptions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.64.020 
Landing fees - penalties.</b>  Aircraft operating in accordance with this
chapter are subject to a landing fee in an amount specified in K.C.C.
4A.700.870.  Failure to pay airport rates, charges and fees or rents may, at
the sole discretion of the airport manager, result in a loss of use of airport
facilities and legal action to recover unpaid rates, charges or fees.  [Airport
late fees and penalties shall be assessed in the amount of one and one-half
percent per month for unpaid rates, charges or fees.  Failure to pay airport
rates, charges and fees or rents shall result in a loss of use of airport
facilities.]*  (Ord. 17919 § 7, 2014:  Ord. 16244 § 8, 2008:  Ord. 16217 § 57,
2008 [repealed by Ord. 16244 § 12, 2008]:  Ord. 15954 § 4, 2007:  Ord. 15639 §
6, 2006:  Ord. 15315 § 6, 2005:  Ord. 15061 § 6, 2004:  Ord. 3382 § 20, 1977: 
Ord. 1159 Art. XVI § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Reviser's note: Material
not included in Ordinance 17919 § 7 but not deleted as required by K.C.C.
1.24.075.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.64.030  Monthly
report.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Monthly reports containing all data required to
determine airport charges, if required, shall be prepared and signed by an
official representative of the owner and/or operator of aircraft operating
pursuant to this chapter and submitted to the airport manager by the tenth day
of the following month.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XVI § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.64.040  Payment.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Payment of charges pursuant to this chapter shall be made prior to the
departure of aircraft, unless arrangements have been approved by the airport
manager.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XVI § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.64.050  Schedule
defined.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The term &quot;schedule&quot; shall mean proposed
regular departure of an aircraft at a specified time, daily or periodically,
during a calendar month (legally filed with the appropriate agencies and
approved by them).  Scheduled airline shall include all air-taxi, commuter,
third-level and other scheduled airlines utilizing the facilities at B.F.I. for
the purpose of enplaning and/or deplaning revenue passengers or carrying
freight, mail, or cargo on a scheduled basis.  (Ord. 3382 § 19, 1977).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.64.060 
Passenger terminal user fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A passenger terminal
user fee in the amount of one dollar per deplaning passenger shall be charged
to the owner or operator of aircraft with a passenger seating capacity of ten
or greater operating pursuant to this chapter.  This fee shall apply to passenger
deplanement made through or into the passenger terminal building or buildings
on B.F.I.  (Ord. 16244 § 9, 2008:  Ord. 16217 § 58, 2008 [repealed by Ord.
16244 § 12, 2008]:  Ord. 3382 § 21, 1977).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.64.070 
Landing fees - exemptions.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  Aircraft,
based or not based at the airport, and operated for hire or compensation or
engaged in commercial business activity, regardless of weight, shall pay a
landing fee based on the aircraft certificated maximum gross landing weight as
published in the manufacturer's aircraft operating manual.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  The
following exemptions to the landing fee apply:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  General
aviation aircraft based at the airport, regardless of weight and with a King
County airport lease, agreement or permit are exempt from the landing fee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  General
aviation aircraft that are not airport based but are using the airport, and
that are twelve thousand five hundred pounds and under as published in the
manufacturer's aircraft operating manual and are not for hire or provided
compensation or engaged in commercial business activity, such as scheduled and
other certificated air carriers, aircraft charters, air-taxi, air cargo, air
courier, air travel clubs and air ambulance are exempt from the landing fee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Aircraft
based at the airport and operated by flight schools or operated for the purpose
of flight instruction and performing &quot;touch and go landings&quot; by which
an aircraft lands and departs on a runway without stopping or exiting the runway
shall be charged a landing fee only if the aircraft exits the runway;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4. 
Humanitarian flights, also known as angel flights, which are operated as
not-for-profit or nonrevenue generating flights for humanitarian, medical or
disaster relief purposes are exempt from the landing fee; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Any
aircraft exempt under state or federal statute or regulatory code is exempt
from the landing fee.  (Ord. 16244 § 10, 2008:  Ord. 16217 § 59, 2008 [repealed
by Ord. 16244 § 12, 2008]:  Ord. 3382 § 22, 1977).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301808"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.72  GROUND
RENTALS</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.72.010     Rates specified.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.72.020     Lease defined.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.72.030     Physical improvements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.72.040     Utilities and other services.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.72.050     Payment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.72.010  Rates
specified.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  [With the exception of rental rate adjustments in this
section, g]round* space on airport property shall be leased in accordance with
K.C.C. chapter 4.56 and the rental rate shall be based upon fair market rental
value as required by chapter 4.56 of this code.  Annual rent adjustments for
intervening years between fair market value appraisals may be established using
the most-recent Consumer Price Index for the Seattle-Tacoma-Bremerton urban
area - all urban consumers.  The Consumer Price Index rent adjustment shall not
be greater than six percent above the amount charged during the prior year and
in no cases shall be less than the amount charged for the prior year.  If the
rent adjustment is made due to a new fair market value appraisal, and that
value is greater than the prior year's rent, then the new fair market value
appraisal becomes the new rent, and the new base for the application of future
Consumer Price Index adjustments.  If the new fair market value appraisal is
less than the prior year's Consumer Price Index-adjusted rent, then the prior
year's Consumer Price Index-adjusted rent shall remain in effect and shall
become the new base rent.  Rents shall be adjusted on January 1 of each year.  (Ord.
17919 § 9, 2014:  Ord. 3382 § 24, 1977: Ord. 1159, Art. XVIII § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Reviser's note:  Material
added in Ordinance 17919 but not displayed as required by K.C.C. 1.24.075.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.72.020  Lease
defined.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Lease&quot; as defined means ground space
acquired for a minimum of one year under legal agreement with King County. 
(Ord. 1159, Art. XVIII § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.72.030  Physical
improvements.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Physical improvements may be constructed at the expense
of the tenant, but only if the location and type of construction has prior
written approval of the airport manager and in accordance with airport minimum
standards.  Tenants must, at all times, maintain physical improvements in good
condition and in conformity with the requirements of King County.  (Ord. 16217
§ 60, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. XVIII § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.72.040  Utilities
and other services.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Utilities and other services which may be required by
the tenant in the rental area shall be paid for by the tenant unless otherwise
provided.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XVIII § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.72.050  Payment.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
All rental charges shall be due and payable in advance.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XVIII
§ 5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301809"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.76  HANGARS AND
OFFICES - COUNTY-OWNED</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.76.010   Rates specified.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.76.020   Physical improvements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.76.030   Payment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.76.040   Utilities and other services -
payment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.76.010 
Rates specified.</b>  Hangar space and office space in county-owned facilities
will be leased or rented based upon the rental rate and terms established from
time to time by King County.  Airport property rental rate shall be based upon
fair market rental value as required by K.C.C. chapter 4.56.  A hangar wait
list shall be maintained by the airport and a one time wait list application
fee of one-hundred dollars shall be charged.  The wait list application fee
shall be applied to the first monthly rental charge.  A nonrefundable annual
fee of ten dollars shall be charged hangar wait list applicants to cover list
administrative costs.  (Ord. 16244 § 11, 2008:  Ord. 16217 § 61, 2008 [repealed
by Ord. 16244 § 12, 2008]:  Ord. 1159, Art XIX, § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.76.020  Physical
improvements.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Tenants must, at all times, maintain physical
improvements in good condition and in conformity with the requirements of King
County.  No improvements or physical changes in the area leased or rented shall
be made without prior written approval of the airport manager.  (Ord. 1159,
Art. XIX § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.76.030  Payment.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Prompt payment for space rented or leased on B.F.I. shall be made in accordance
with the terms and conditions of the agreement.  (Ord. 1159, Art. XIX § 3,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>15.76.040 
Utilities and other services - payment.</b>  Utilities and other services that
may be required by the tenant in the rental area or facilities shall be paid
for by the tenant unless otherwise provided. (Ord. 16217 § 62, 2008).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301810"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.80  PENALTIES</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>(Formerly PENALTIES AND
CONSTRUCTION OF TITLE)</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.80.010     Violators
prohibited use of airport.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.80.020     Penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.80.010  Violators
prohibited use of airport.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person, including any person who
operates or handles any aircraft, operates any vehicle, equipment or apparatus,
who fails to comply with airport rules or regulations, or is determined to be
delinquent in the person's payment for the use of airport facilities, may be
promptly removed from the airport by or under the authority of the airport
manager; and may be deprived of, or refused the further use of, the airport,
and its facilities for such length of time as may be determined by either the
airport manager or the King County council, or both.  (Ord. 18670 § 73, 2018:  Ord.
1159, Art. XXI § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.80.020  Penalties.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Violation
of this chapter constitutes an infraction violation and the punishment shall be
as provided by the laws of King County or the state of Washington.  Regulatory
infractions such as building and fire code or use shall be corrected by the
leaseholder.  Failure to correct infractions will result in loss of use of
airport facilities.  (Ord. 16217 § 63, 2008:  Ord. 1159, Art. XXI § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301811"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.90  MUSEUM OF
FLIGHT AUTHORITY</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.010     Authority created.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.020     Name.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.030     Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.040     Powers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.050     Charter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.060     Effect of issuance of charter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.070     Board of directors.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.080     Organization of board of directors.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.090     Bylaws.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.100     Quorum.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.110     Dissolution.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.120     Board removal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.130     Ancillary authority.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        15.90.140     Construction.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.010  Authority
created.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  AUTHORITY
CREATED.  A public authority is hereby created, with powers and limitations as
set forth in its charter and this chapter, exclusively to undertake, assist
with and otherwise facilitate or provide for the development and operation of a
first class air and space museum as authorized under RCW 35.21.730 through
35.21.755.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  COUNTY
LIABILITY LIMITED.  The authority is an independent legal entity exclusively
responsible for its own debts, obligations and liabilities.  All liabilities
incurred by the authority shall be satisfied exclusively from the assets and
credit of the authority; no creditor or other person shall have any recourse to
the assets, credit, or services of the county on account of any debts,
obligations, liabilities, acts or omissions of the authority.  (Ord. 7444 § 1,
1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.020  Name.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The name of the public authority shall be the King County Museum of Flight
Authority.  (Ord. 7444 § 2, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.030 
Definitions.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The definitions in this section apply throughout this
chapter unless the context clearly requires otherwise.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  &quot;Board
of directors&quot; or &quot;board&quot; means the governing body vested with
the management of the affairs of the public authority.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  &quot;Bylaws&quot;
means the rules adopted for the regulation or management of the affairs of the
public authority adopted by this chapter and all subsequent amendments thereto.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  &quot;Charter&quot;
means the articles of organization of the public authority adopted by this
chapter and all subsequent amendments thereto.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  &quot;Council
clerk&quot; means the clerk of the King County council or a person authorized
to act on the council clerk's behalf; and in the event of reorganization of the
office of council clerk, the successor official performing such duties or a
person authorized to act on the successor's behalf.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E. 
&quot;County&quot; means King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          F.  &quot;County
council&quot; means the body established under Article 2 of the King County
Charter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          G.  &quot;County
executive&quot; means the county executive of King County, as established by
Article 3 of the King County Charter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          H. 
&quot;Director&quot; means a member of the board.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          I.  &quot;Public
authority&quot; or &quot;authority&quot; means the authority created under this
ordinance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          J.  &quot;Resolution&quot;
means an action of the board with the quorum required in K.C.C. 15.90.100.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          K.  &quot;State,&quot;
when used as a noun, means the state of Washington.  (Ord. 18670 § 74, 2018:  Ord.
7444 § 3, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.040  Powers.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Except as limited by the state constitution, the King County Charter, this
chapter, or the charter of the public authority, the public authority shall
have and may exercise all lawful powers necessary or convenient to effect the
purposes for which the public authority is organized and to perform authorized
corporate functions, as provided in its charter.  (Ord. 7444 § 4, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.050  Charter.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The charter of the authority, Exhibit A* of Ordinance 7444, is hereby
approved.  The charter shall be issued in duplicate originals, each bearing the
county seal attested by the council clerk.  One original shall be recorded with
the records and licensing services division, or its successor agency; a
duplicate original shall be provided to the authority.  The charter shall be
amended only by county ordinance adopted at or after a public hearing held with
notice to the public authority and authority directors and affording them a
reasonable opportunity to be heard and present testimony.  (Ord. 15971 § 84,
2007:  Ord. 14498 § 23, 2002:  Ord. 14176 § 2, 2001:  Ord. 7444 § 5, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;background:white'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>*Available in the King County Archives.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.060  Effect
of issuance of charter.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The public authority shall commence
its existence effective upon issuance of its charter.  Except as against the
state or the county in a proceeding to cancel or revoke the charter, delivery
of a duplicate original charter shall conclusively establish that the public
authority has been established in compliance with the procedures of this chapter. 
(Ord. 7444 § 6, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.070  Board
of directors.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A board consisting of seven directors (the &quot;board
of directors&quot;) is hereby established to govern the affairs of the public
authority.  The directors shall be appointed and serve their terms as provided
in the charter.  All corporate powers of the public authority shall be
exercised by or under the authority of the board of directors; and the
business, property and affairs of the authority shall be managed under the
direction of the board of directors, except as may be otherwise provided for by
law or in the charter.  (Ord. 7444 § 7, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.90.080  Organization
of board of directors.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Upon issuance of the charter, the
county executive or designee shall call an organizational meeting of the
initial board of directors within ten days, giving at least three days' advance
written notice to each, unless waived in writing.  At such meeting, the board
shall organize itself, may appoint officers and select the place of business. 
(Ord. 18670 § 75, 2018:  Ord. 14199 § 221, 2001:  Ord. 7444 § 8, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          15.90.090 
Bylaws.</span></b></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  The
initial bylaws (the &quot;bylaws&quot;) of the public authority, Exhibit B of Ordinance
7444*, are hereby approved.  The power to alter, amend, or repeal the bylaws or
adopt new ones shall be vested in the board except as otherwise provided in the
charter.  The bylaws shall be consistent with the charter.</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  As
necessary and appropriate, the county council may amend the authority bylaws by
ordinance adopted at or after a public hearing held with notice to the public
authority and authority directors and affording them a reasonable opportunity
to be heard and present testimony.  (Ord. 7444 §9, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=footnote style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Available in the King County Archives.</span></b></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          15.90.100 
Quorum.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>  At all
meetings of the board of directors, a majority of the board of directors then
in office shall constitute a quorum.  (Ord. 7444 § 10, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          15.90.110 
Dissolution.</span></b></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  If the
county council makes an affirmative finding that dissolution is warranted for
any reason, the existence of a public authority may be terminated by ordinance
of the county council adopted at or after a public hearing, held with notice to
the public authority and authority directors and affording them a reasonable
opportunity to be heard and present testimony.  Dissolution shall be
accomplished as provided in the charter and shall not take effect until proper
provision has been made for disposition of all authority assets.</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  Upon
satisfactory completion of dissolution proceedings, the council clerk shall
indicate such dissolution by inscription of &quot;charter canceled&quot; on the
original charter of the public authority, on file with the county and, when
available, on the duplicate original of the public authority, and the existence
of the public authority shall cease.  The council clerk shall give notice
thereof pursuant to state law and to other persons requested by the public
authority in its dissolution statement.</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          C.  Upon
dissolution of the authority and the winding up of its affairs, title to all
remaining assets or property of the authority shall vest in King County unless
the county council or trustee or court has provided for the transfer of any
authority rights, assets or property to a qualified entity or entities which
will fulfill the purposes for which the authority was chartered.  (Ord. 7444 §
11, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          15.90.120 
Board removal.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>  If it
is determined for any reason that any or all of the board members should be
removed from office, after a full public hearing, the county may by ordinance
remove any or all voting board members from office. The term of any board
member removed pursuant to this section shall expire when the removal ordinance
takes effect.  Vacancies created under this section shall be filled in the same
manner as provided in the charter.  (Ord. 7444 § 12, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          15.90.130 
Ancillary authority.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'> 
The county executive is granted all such power and authority as reasonably
necessary or convenient to enable the county executive to administer this
chapter efficiently and to perform the duties imposed in this chapter or the
authority charter.  (<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 18670 § 76, 2018: 
</span>Ord. 7444 § 13, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=tx><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          15.90.140 
Construction.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>  This
chapter shall be liberally construed so as to effectuate its purposes and the
purposes of RCW 35.21.730.755.  (Ord. 7444 § 14, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=tx><u><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301812"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.94  AIRPORT
ROUNDTABLE</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.94.010     Establishment
and composition.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.94.020     Scope
and charge.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.94.030     Appointment
and terms.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.94.040     Administrative
support.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.94.050     Compensation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <b>15.94.010  Establishment and
composition.</b>  The King County Airport roundtable, which, for the purposes
of this chapter, is also known as &quot;the roundtable,&quot; is hereby
established. It shall be comprised of eighteen regular voting members
representing the following interests: ten representatives of communities
directly affected by the airport, including one each from Georgetown, Magnolia
or North Seattle, Tukwila, Renton/Kent/South King County, Beacon Hill, Rainier
Valley, West Seattle, unincorporated King County, South Park and one at-large;
four airport tenant representatives, one each from a cargo operator or
scheduled air carrier, small general aviation and corporate tenants and one
from Boeing; one representative from a pilots' association; one representative
from a commercial enterprise that is an off-site user or an off-site provider
of airport-related services; and two labor representatives. In addition, the
Federal Aviation Administration may designate one ex officio nonvoting member.  (Ord.
19713 § 2, 2023:  <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 16217 § 65, 2008:</span> 
Ord. 12785 § 1, 1997).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <b>15.94.020  Scope and charge.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  The roundtable shall advise and
make recommendations to the airport management, county executive and county
council on the airport budget, programs, regulations, master plans and noise
reduction strategies and other related matters.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  The roundtable shall adopt bylaws
and operating rules consistent with this chapter and other applicable county
policies by a majority vote of its members.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          C.  If approved by a majority of
roundtable members, the roundtable may appoint subcommittees.  Subcommittee
membership may include representatives who are not regular members of the
roundtable.  In appointing any subcommittee, the roundtable shall reflect the
charge to the subcommittee in the minutes of the meeting at which the decision
was made and shall indicate in the minutes whether the subcommittee is intended
to be a standing subcommittee or an ad hoc subcommittee for a limited
duration.  (Ord. 12785 § 2, 1997).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <b>15.94.030  Appointment and terms.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  Except for the five members
representing Georgetown, Tukwila, Beacon Hill, Rainier Valley, and South Park,
regular members, as defined in K.C.C. 15.94.010, shall be appointed by the
county executive subject to confirmation by the county council by motion. The
executive may appoint nonvoting ex officio members who shall serve at the
executive's discretion.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  The five members representing
Georgetown, Tukwila, Beacon Hill, Rainier Valley, and South Park shall be
nominated for appointment by the executive in consultation with the elected
representative or representatives of the community's respective county council
district or districts and approved by motion of the county council and may be
reappointed by the executive in consultation with the elected representative or
representatives of the community's respective county council district or
districts to serve up to two full consecutive terms, subject to confirmation by
the council by motion.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          C.  Except as otherwise provided in
subsection B. of this section, members may be reappointed by the executive to
serve up to two full consecutive terms, subject to confirmation by the council by
motion.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          D.  Representatives of Boeing and
labor are exempt from term limits.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          E.  Members shall serve a term of
three years or until their successor is appointed and confirmed as provided in
this chapter. The terms of office shall be staggered consistent with K.C.C. chapter
2.28.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          F.  A vacancy shall be filled for the
remainder of the term of the vacant position in the manner described in the
initial appointment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          G.  A majority of the committee shall
elect one of its members as chair.  The term of the chair shall be for one year
and the chair shall not serve more than two consecutive terms as chair.  (Ord.
19713 § 3, 2023:  Ord. 16641 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 1,
2009:  Ord. 12785 § 3, 1997).</span></p>

<p class=tx><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <b>15.94.040  Administrative support.</b> 
The airport manager shall be responsible for convening, facilitating and
providing administrative support to the roundtable.  (<span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>Ord. 16217 § 67, 2008:</span>  Ord. 12785 § 4, 1997).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <b>15.94.050  Compensation.</b>  In
accordance with K.C.C. 2.28.006, members of the roundtable who are neither
employees of King County nor employees of other municipal governments may
receive per diem compensation.  The purpose is to compensate community members
for contributing their experience and expertise to the roundtable.  Payment of
compensation shall comply with federal obligations.  (Ord. 19713 § 4, 2023:  Ord.
12785 § 5, 1997).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc422301813"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>15.96  SECURITY
PROGRAM - REQUIREMENTS - FEE</span></a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          15.96.010   Security program - requirements -
fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          <b>15.96.010  Security program -
requirements - fee. </b>  The airport shall maintain a security program in
compliance with F.A.A. and Transportation Security Administration guidance. 
The airport shall maintain an access control system for airfield and building
security.  The airfield and building access control system shall include a
badge system for employees, tenants, tenant employees, vendors, suppliers,
contractors and guests.  Airport employees, tenants and other personnel are
required to obtain and display an airport issued photo identification badge
while at the airport and in airport regulated buildings.  All badges are the
property of the airport and shall be returned to the airport operations and
compliance office upon termination of leases, employment or other activity. 
The airport may impose an administrative fee as part of the annual county
budget process for issuing airport badges.  The airport shall impose an
administrative fee of twenty-five dollars for replacement of lost, stolen or
nonreturned security badges.  (<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 16217 §
68, 2008).</span></span></p>

